cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "amr-clonalshare: measuring how much of antimicrobial resistance travels with the clone"
abstract: >-
  Estimates the share of variance in an antimicrobial resistance phenotype
  that the lineages of a bacterial collection carry, from a lineage label and
  a susceptibility call or a recorded dilution, and refuses the estimate
  where the collection cannot support one. One collection admits three
  quantities and the package reports them apart, each with its own interval:
  the lineage-membership share, what a rule scored out of sample reaches; the
  design-corrected component ratio of the same collection, with an interval
  exact under the Gaussian one-way model by inversion of a noncentral F; and a
  superpopulation share for the species. Each is scored against its own truth
  on 135 simulated cells from five lineages to a thousand, and each sits
  behind a gate that refuses where the collection cannot identify the quantity
  or the residuals contradict the law the interval assumes, with a
  binary share restated on the latent scale beside the observed scale; the lineage label may
  be a sequence type, a core-genome or SNP cluster, or a serovar, so the same
  estimate can be read at two typing resolutions.
  A second family of outputs decomposes a difference in non-wild-type
  prevalence between two collections into a lineage-composition and a
  within-lineage rate component using the Kitagawa identity, with a calibrated
  estimability gate on shared lineage support, a test for lineage labels that
  are differentially and informatively missing, and Benjamini-Yekutieli
  control within each component family, valid whatever the dependence between
  agents, beside the effective number of independent agents. Prevalence is reported on both the isolate and the lineage scale.
  A third family of outputs reads a susceptibility panel at its recorded
  resolution: a dichotomised call and a recorded dilution are both intervals on
  the log2 concentration scale and enter one interval likelihood, so the input
  mode changes how much an observation carries rather than what is estimated.
  Each share also carries an e-value, and a programme of yearly intakes a
  sequential e-value whose running product is a test supermartingale, with
  false-discovery control across the panel that holds under arbitrary
  dependence between antimicrobials. The attribution is exercised outside the shipped cohorts on
  fifty organisms of one NCBI Pathogen Detection release, each taken at the
  release accession the retrieval recorded, where 192 agent cells are
  estimated in twelve species and 44 admitted by the support gate in six, each
  with a permuted-label control, on the same release cut by host and sampling
  matrix, with 131 Salmonella cells read at two typing resolutions, and on the
  Streptococcus suis cohort at three definitions of a lineage. The package reads two tables and never a
  genome.
